        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cherry_grove_ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Today, Cherry Grove is a suburban neighborhood known for its single‑family homes and local parks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cherry_grove_ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cherry Grove sits in the Little Miami River watershed, part of the larger Ohio River basin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cherry_grove_ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers erected blockhouses at Gerrard's Station near the Little Miami River mouth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cherry_grove_ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cherry Grove experiences a temperate continental climate with July highs near 85°F and January lows around 25°F.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
